Proposal only (ws341-p001). Makefile and mk/ are not changed by agents; this diff waits for the
user's approval (plan/ws341/user-questions.md, question 6).  Line positions are against main 44bb7cdaac;
the source file list follows the design (src/drivers/gpu/vgpu/) and may change with p004.

--- a/mk/config.mk
+++ b/mk/config.mk
@@ (after the [Venus GPU Driver] block)
 CONFIG_DRIVER_PCI_VENUS           ?= n

+# [Virtual display driver (/dev/vgpu)]
+#  - Depends: CONFIG_DRIVER_GPU
+CONFIG_DRIVER_VGPU                ?= n
+
 ########################
 # Legacy 2D Drivers
 ########################
--- a/mk/kernel.mk
+++ b/mk/kernel.mk
@@ (after the [Venus GPU Driver] block)
 	src/drivers/gpu/venus/share.c
 endif

+# [Virtual display driver]
+ifneq ($(filter y,$(CONFIG_DRIVER_VGPU)),)
+KERN_CPPFLAGS += -DCONFIG_DRIVER_VGPU=1
+KERN_SOURCES += \
+	src/drivers/gpu/vgpu/vgpu.c \
+	src/drivers/gpu/vgpu/display.c \
+	src/drivers/gpu/vgpu/frame.c
+endif
+
 # [Boot Linear Framebuffer driver]
--- a/mk/platform-x86_64/defaults.mk
+++ b/mk/platform-x86_64/defaults.mk
@@
 CONFIG_DRIVER_PCI_VENUS           := y
+CONFIG_DRIVER_VGPU                := y
 CONFIG_DRIVER_AUDIO               := y
--- a/mk/platform-rpi4/defaults.mk, mk/platform-rpi5/defaults.mk, mk/platform-vf2/defaults.mk
+++ (each, next to its CONFIG_DRIVER_GPU line)
+CONFIG_DRIVER_VGPU                := y
--- a/config/drivers/generic.drivers
+++ b/config/drivers/generic.drivers
@@
 -|fixed|Loop block device|*|y|
+CONFIG_DRIVER_VGPU|bool|Virtual display for remote screens (/dev/vgpu)|amd64,rpi4,rpi5,visionfive2|y|
--- a/config/drivers/menu.list
+++ b/config/drivers/menu.list
@@
-GPU|CONFIG_DRIVER_PCI_VENUS CONFIG_DRIVER_PCI_I915 CONFIG_DRIVER_PCI_NVRTX CONFIG_DRIVER_PCI_AMDRDNA CONFIG_DRIVER_PCI_GHCI
+GPU|CONFIG_DRIVER_PCI_VENUS CONFIG_DRIVER_PCI_I915 CONFIG_DRIVER_PCI_NVRTX CONFIG_DRIVER_PCI_AMDRDNA CONFIG_DRIVER_PCI_GHCI CONFIG_DRIVER_VGPU

Notes:
- The three important platforms (x86_64, arm64, riscv64) default to y, so that every change is
  build-checked on them and the QEMU (Venus) images carry the driver for p005 and p009.  Question 4
  asks whether the user's builds should carry it by default.
- Not in this diff, also needing approval before their phases: the Makefiles of the userland test
  programs and the tool (userland/tests/vgpu-loop, the Vulkan compositor stand-in, vgpu-capture),
  proposed in p005 and p009 in the same form as the existing userland/tests/*/Makefile.
- The driver registers its display node only after a render node exists (design §3.1), so a kernel
  with the driver and no GPU has no extra /dev/gpuN.
- The device number of /dev/vgpu is chosen in p004a (not a make variable).
